---
description: Nebula shared work log — read before a task, append after
alwaysApply: true
---

This repo keeps a shared work log at `.claude/MEMORY.md`: one entry per task, recording what was asked,
what was actually done, and the gotchas hit along the way.

**Before starting a task**, read `.claude/MEMORY.md` and scan for entries related to what the user is
asking — the same crate, subsystem, symptom, or tool. A recorded gotcha is a mine already stepped on; a
recorded decision is settled unless the user reopens it. Entries describe what was true when written, so
confirm any file or flag they name still exists before relying on it.

**After finishing a task** that changed code or behavior, diagnosed a bug, or turned up something
non-obvious, read `.claude/skills/nebula-memory/SKILL.md` and follow it to append an entry. Skip it for
pure questions and trivial edits — the log is only useful if it stays free of restated diffs.
